# A second REAL process on the same locks (the spec uses a second `open()` of the same file in one process, which `flock` also treats
# as another owner). A holder process takes the lock files with `fcntl.flock(f, LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB)` and sleeps; then each runner is
# started as a command from the worktree (it never gets past the lock: no git, no rustc, no cargo, no measurement is asked for;
# the tree was dirty, so a build phase would have refused before building even if a lock had been free by accident); then the
